{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#124","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#124","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#124\",\"parent_revision\":\"85ef8ba6d9c03d36ac2b164cc66ccc9f4d2e385b7d2ad30bb16a02a77f80f14a\",\"root_revision\":\"85ef8ba6d9c03d36ac2b164cc66ccc9f4d2e385b7d2ad30bb16a02a77f80f14a\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nSome rules register metadata in one place and detect in another. `check_lk001` returns `[]` and exists purely so `RULE_REGISTRY` carries its metadata, while detection lives in `InternalLinkValidator`.\\n\\nNothing asserts the two agree. No gate checks that a registered rule code with a stub function has a corresponding emitter, or that the stub's docstring matches the emitter's actual behaviour.\\n\\nThis is live right now: `check_lk001`'s docstring documents the `${CLAUDE_*}` substitution behaviour added in #122. It is accurate today, and keeping it accurate is manual.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA registry-level test asserting every stub-backed code appears in at least one emitter call site would catch drift cheaply.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- #122 \u2014 added the `${CLAUDE_*}` behaviour the docstring now describes\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"097df5cbd1e12f5f8526a12ec84625623db4340d96220a71a00c6dca3ca09d8b\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDORXxKvc8AAAABXP-E7w\"}"}